-- Difficulty: Easy
-- Pattern:    main pattern (and a second one, if any)
-- Trick:      use a subquery in the where clause
-- Gotcha:     
-- Solved:     2026-10-16
-- Re-solved cold: YYYY-MM-DD

-- two tables: pages and page_likes, both containing a page_id column. the page_id column of page_likes table only contains pages that have at least one "like" from a user
-- therefore any value from the page_id column of the "pages" table that is not in the "page_likes" table, have no likes. Use a subquery to filter that value.

SELECT
  P.page_id
FROM pages P
WHERE P.page_id NOT IN (SELECT PL.page_id FROM page_likes PL)
ORDER BY P.page_id ASC
